<title>CYPRUS: Cyprus March CPI increases 2.78 pct mnth/mnth.</title>
<headline>Cyprus March CPI increases 2.78 pct mnth/mnth.</headline>
<dateline>NICOSIA 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cyprus's consumer price index increased by 2.78 percent in March to 119.47 compared to 116.24 in February, the island's statistics and research department announced.</p>
<p>    Consumer price index	March 97  Feb 97   March 96</p>
<p>    Month/month change (pct)    2.78   -1.55	2.66</p>
<p>    Year/year change (pct)	3.67    3.55	3.28</p>
<p>    Index (92=100)		119.47   116.24    115.24</p>
<p>The department attributed the rise to an increase in the retail prices of clothing, footwear and furniture after the end of the winter sales period in February and to increases in the price of electricity and certain fresh vegetables.</p>
<p>-- Nicosia newsroom 357 2 365089</p>
